        "title": "Electromagnetic Spectrum and Atmospheric Windows",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every remote sensing system exploits a specific region of the EM spectrum where: (1) the atmosphere is reasonably transparent, and (2) the surface emits or reflects enough energy to detect. Understanding which windows exist, what blocks them, and what physical process dominates each region is the physics foundation for everything else in remote sensing."
    },
